## chore(review): repair the live scenario campaign and the Sphinx build

Context: a full review pass — run every suite including the opt-in live
scenario campaign, then audit code and docs against `.cursorrules` and
`src/.coding_rules.md`. Two things were actually broken, both silently:
the scenario campaign could not create its domain, and the Sphinx build was
dropping roughly a third of the API reference without failing.

### 1. Scenario campaign — domain name rejected by CamelCase validation

The campaign used the domain name `test_scenario_1`, which
`is_valid_domain_name` (`^[A-Z][a-zA-Z0-9]*$`) has rejected since CamelCase
enforcement was added on creation. Scenario 1 failed at `POST /domain/info`
with a 400, and scenarios 2, 3 and validation skipped because they depend on
it — so the whole campaign had been dead, not merely unrun.

Domain *names* and registry *folders* are different strings (the folder is the
sanitized lowercase form and is what appears in registry listings and REST
paths). The suites conflated them into a single constant, so the fix separates
the two rather than just renaming.

1. `tests/e2e/scenarios/test_scenario_01_generate_live.py`
   `_DOMAIN_NAME = "TestScenario1"` for creation and assertions, plus a new
   `_DOMAIN_FOLDER` (its lowercase form) for the registry lookup, the delete
   path, and the final listing assertion.
2. `tests/e2e/scenarios/test_scenario_02_collab_lifecycle.py`,
   `test_scenario_03_rules_analysis.py`, `test_scenario_validation.py`
   These only ever use the value as a registry folder, so the
   `ONTOBRICKS_SCENARIO_DOMAIN` default becomes `testscenario1`.
3. `tests/e2e/scenarios/README.md`
   Documents the name/folder distinction so the next author does not re-merge
   them.

### 2. Sphinx build — `pyarrow` must not be mocked

`autodoc_mock_imports` listed `pyarrow`. `pandas` is pulled in transitively by
`neo4j._optional_deps` and evaluates `Version(pyarrow.__version__)` at import
time, which raises `TypeError` on a mock object. Thirty modules — every HTML
route, every internal router, the graphdb backends, `shared.fastapi.main` —
failed to import and were emitted as empty stubs behind a `--keep-going`
warning nobody read.

4. `docs/sphinx/conf.py`
   Dropped `pyarrow` from the mock list (with a comment explaining why it must
   stay out), added `myst_heading_anchors = 4` so the `file.md#heading` links
   used throughout `/docs` resolve at all, read `release`/`version` from
   `pyproject.toml` instead of the hard-coded and long-stale `0.1.1`,
   registered `mermaid`/`csv` as plain-text lexers, and suppressed
   `misc.highlighting_failure` (the Turtle lexer rejects legal prefixed names
   such as `ex:person/p1`, costing ~100 warnings that buried the real ones).

### 3. Docs that were absent, mis-linked or mis-rendered

5. `docs/sphinx/guides/{code_organization,lakebase-graphdb,graphdb-integration,cohort_discovery,features,sizing}.md`
   New include wrappers; six substantive guides existed in `/docs` but were in
   no toctree, so they were never published and every link into them broke.
   Registered in `docs/sphinx/index.rst`.
6. `docs/sphinx/api/app.core.industry.rst`, `api_external.rst`
   Pointed at modules renamed long ago (`*.service` → `*ImportService`,
   `api.routers.projects` → `api.routers.domains`); FHIR was missing entirely.
7. `docs/sizing.md`
   Fifteen fill-in blanks were bare underscore runs on their own line, which
   Markdown renders as horizontal rules — on GitHub as well as in Sphinx. Now
   wrapped in code spans so they render as blanks.
8. `docs/get-started.md`, `docs/architecture.md`, `docs/lakebase-graphdb.md`
   Broken anchors repaired (`#data-quality`, `#reasoning`,
   `#ontoviz---visual-ontology-editor`, `#9-digital-twin-build--step-by-step`
   — the last two stale from the OntoViz and Digital-Twin→Knowledge-Graph
   renames).
9. `docs/screenshots/*.png`, `docs/INFO.md`, `docs/architecture.md`
   Renamed the three screenshots containing spaces; MyST percent-encodes the
   destination, so `Ontology%20design.png` never resolved.
10. `docs/sphinx/api/app.core.{errors,sqlwizard,rst}`,
    `app.core.graphdb.{neo4j,lakebase}.rst`, `app.core.external.pitfalls.rst`
    Package-level `automodule` directives re-documented the classes their
    per-module directives already own; marked `:no-index:` (18 duplicate-object
    warnings).
11. `docs/sphinx/api/app.objects.{digitaltwin,mapping,ontology,session}.rst`
    Title underlines were one character short. The digitaltwin title also still
    said "Digital twin".
12. Docstring RST repairs in `src/` — missing blank line before a bullet or
    enumerated list, and inline literals that never closed:
    `back/core/databricks/lakebase/LakebaseAuth.py`,
    `back/core/graphdb/lakebase/_companion_ddl.py` (`*_sync` opened RST
    emphasis), `back/objects/domain/SettingsService.py`,
    `back/objects/ontology/Ontology.py`,
    `back/objects/registry/PermissionService.py`,
    `api/routers/internal/ontology.py`.
13. `.cursor/08-testing-and-deployment.mdc`, `ci/build_docs.sh`
    The rule told agents to run `scripts/build_docs.sh`, which does not exist —
    the script is `ci/build_docs.sh`, and its own usage header was wrong too.
14. `src/back/core/graphdb/lakebase/SyncedTableManager.py`
    `:doc:`/graphdb-integration`` → `/guides/graphdb-integration`.

Sphinx warnings: 198 → 14. The remaining 14 are 11 repo-relative links that
resolve on GitHub but point outside the Sphinx tree (`../src/`, `../tests/`,
`../data/`), and 3 ambiguous cross-references where an attribute named
`object` and eight classes named `AgentResult` shadow the intended targets.

